+/// Depth-adaptive first-try aspiration half-width (centipawns). Starts at
+/// `ASPIRATION_BASE_HALF_WIDTH` at the threshold depth and narrows by
+/// `ASPIRATION_WIDTH_SLOPE` per ply beyond it, clamped at
+/// `ASPIRATION_MIN_HALF_WIDTH`. Item B (tuning-backlog, depth-adaptive tier).
+///
+/// Monotone non-increasing in `depth`; equals the base at `depth ==
+/// ASPIRATION_MIN_DEPTH` (so the threshold behavior is unchanged from M4.D's
+/// fixed ±50). `depth < ASPIRATION_MIN_DEPTH` never reaches here (the caller
+/// short-circuits to the full window first), but the `saturating_sub` keeps the
+/// function total and well-defined for any input.
+///
+/// Pure function.
+fn aspiration_half_width(depth: u32) -> i32 {
+    let steps = depth.saturating_sub(ASPIRATION_MIN_DEPTH) as i32;
+    (ASPIRATION_BASE_HALF_WIDTH - ASPIRATION_WIDTH_SLOPE * steps).max(ASPIRATION_MIN_HALF_WIDTH)
+}
